.TH "INPUTS/EXTENSIONS.MD" 7
.SH "Extensions"
.PP
Corpus for Phase 1 markdown constructs added after the initial pipeline. Accumulates across tasks \[u2014] add new sections, don't replace old ones.
.SS "Task lists (T1.1)"
.IP \(bu 2
[ ] unchecked item
.IP \(bu 2
[x] checked item (lowercase x)
.IP \(bu 2
[x] checked item (uppercase X)
.IP \(bu 2
plain bullet item, no checkbox
.IP 1. 4
[ ] first ordered task
.IP 2. 4
[x] second ordered task, done
.IP 3. 4
plain ordered item
.IP \(bu 2
[x] checked item with continuation second line of the same item, indented under the checkbox
.SS "Strikethrough (T1.1)"
.PP
This is deleted text inside a sentence.
.PP
Whole line struck through.
.PP
Mixed \fBbold and struck together\fR.
.SS "Reference links, titles, images (T1.2)"
.PP
Inline link with title: Anthropic (https://www.anthropic.com).
.PP
Reference link: the docs (https://example.com/docs) explain more.
.PP
Collapsed reference: Docs Ref (https://example.com/docs-ref) also works.
.PP
Shortcut reference: Docs Ref (https://example.com/docs-ref) resolves the same way.
.PP
Undefined reference stays literal: [nowhere][missing-ref].
.PP
Undefined shortcut stays literal: [Also Missing].
.PP
Image with title: [image: a small logo] (https://example.com/logo.png)
.PP
Reference image: [image: alt text] (https://example.com/image.png)
.PP
Paren url survives inline: Haskell (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haskell_(programming_language)) stays whole.
.PP
Paren url by reference: the Haskell article (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haskell_(programming_language)).
.PP
Paren-form title: point here (https://example.com/pt) uses (title) syntax.
.SS "Math small fixes (T1.5)"
.PP
Cube root: \[u221B](8). Fourth root: \[u221C](16). Other index: [5]\[u221A](32).
.PP
Plain root unaffected: \[u221A]2.
.PP
Nested content under a cube root: \[u221B](x+y).
.SS "Tables (writer coverage)"
.TS
allbox;
l c r
.
Tool	Year	Notes
\f(CWmhs\fR	2023	MicroHs \fBcompiler\fR
groff	1990	\fIroff\fR successor
.TE
